<h2>What we install</h2>

<p><strong>Baseboards, casings and shoe moulding.</strong> New trim after flooring or drywall work, or a full replacement to update a room. After a Carleton Place basement flood, we installed custom-fit trim around every doorway along with new baseboards and shoe moulding.</p>

<p><strong>Crown moulding.</strong> Crown along a ceiling line or across the top of a built-in, such as the shelving wall we built in a Kanata living room.</p>

<p><strong>Wainscoting, panelling and accent walls.</strong> Panelled or board-and-batten walls, picture-frame moulding and feature walls that give a plain room some character.</p>

<p><strong>Fireplace mantels and surrounds.</strong> From a simple floating shelf to a full traditional mantel. In Perth we designed and built a multi-layered mantel with decorative corbels, an arched header and dentil crown moulding, built on site in the client's garage. It has a large-format tile surround and a raised step hearth.</p>

<p><strong>Interior and closet doors.</strong> Hanging interior doors, bifolds and sliding barn doors, and trimming them out. In one basement we hung two pairs of six-panel bifold doors across a wide storage wall, set out with a laser level so the whole run lines up.</p>

<p><strong>Custom exterior doors and openings.</strong> Larger jobs such as framing a new 8 foot opening with a header for a set of custom double doors on a rural West Carleton outbuilding.</p>

<h2>The details that matter</h2>

<p>Old houses aren't square, and new ones aren't always either. Good trim work means scribing to walls and floors that aren't flat, coping inside corners so they stay tight through the seasons, and keeping reveals consistent around every door. We check level and plumb with a laser rather than trusting the walls, and we fill and caulk so everything is ready for paint.</p>

<h2>Fireplace surrounds</h2>

<p>A fireplace wall is usually the focal point of a room, and it combines several trades: framing or a drywall bump-out, tile, a mantel, trim and paint. In a Carleton Place living room we built out a drywall surround with a recessed niche, a wood sill and baseboard wrapped all the way around, below a floating mantel shelf. On a Kanata fireplace we prepped and primed the existing wood and metal and replaced the grout to refresh the whole surround.</p>

<p>Fireplaces have required clearances between the firebox and combustible materials like wood trim, so the design starts with those and the appliance manufacturer's instructions. Any wiring for outlets in a niche or a wall-mounted TV is done by qualified, certified electricians, whom we arrange as part of the project. Gas work, such as connecting a gas fireplace, isn't included.</p>

<h2>Residential and commercial</h2>

<p>Most of our trim work is in homes, but we also do finish carpentry in condos and commercial spaces: offices, shops and rental units. We've built a custom office desk at a client's workplace (see <a href="{{ url('/services/custom-built-ins-closets') }}">custom built-ins</a>), and our most recent kitchen was a condo project too (see <a href="{{ url('/services/kitchen-remodel') }}">kitchen remodels</a>).</p>

<h2>How a trim job works</h2>

<p>You send photos and tell us what you'd like. We visit to measure and look at the walls, floors and existing trim. Then you get a written estimate in Canadian dollars, labour-only or with materials, along with a schedule. Once the trim is chosen, we install, fill and caulk so it's ready for paint, and clean up. We'll agree on painting or staining as part of the quote. Workmanship is covered by our one-year limited <a href="{{ url('/warranty') }}">warranty</a>.</p>

<h2>Why Zanini Renovations for trim</h2>

<p>Trim is where hurried work shows. We don't rush the finishing or treat it as an afterthought. You deal directly with the owner, Jonas Zanini, from the estimate to the final walkthrough. Zanini Renovations is fully insured.</p>

<h2>Where we work</h2>

<p>We do finish carpentry in Carleton Place, Beckwith, Franktown, Almonte, Pakenham, Perth, Smiths Falls, Arnprior and Lanark Highlands, and across Ottawa: Kanata, Stittsville, Barrhaven, Nepean, Riverside South, Manotick, Richmond, Carp and Ashton. We also work in Gatineau.</p>
